<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hussite Wars</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1419–1434</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Hussite Revolution</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hussite Wars were fought in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a> from 1419 to about 1434 between the followers of the reformer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jan-hus">Jan Hus</a> and Catholic rulers led by Emperor Sigismund. Hussite armies under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jan-zizka">Jan Žižka</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prokop-the-great">Prokop the Great</a>, using wagon forts and firearms, defeated five <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusades</a> sent against them; the moderate Utraquists then defeated the radical Taborites at Lipany (1434) and reached a settlement with the Church.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hussite-wars.jpg" alt="Hussite Wars" width="320" height="451" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hussitenkriege.tif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
